 "concept": "Red-brick Victorian factory complex in the steampunk kit. Silhouette: a tall clock tower is the single landmark, rising from a long sawtooth-roofed machine hall. Hierarchy: the wide 2-storey machine hall (28x20, 11 high) forms the main body. A boiler/furnace house with a chimney attaches east. A lower workshop and lab wing attaches south as an L, and a small octagonal counting-house sits at the west entrance. A bridge crosses the yard gap to a separate storage annex. Materials: red bricks (wall2) with stone-brick piers, cut-copper trim and cornice, a dark deepslate-tile roof, and cyan glass with glowing lantern bands. Detail goes outward only: gears on the hall face, pipes on the process hall, chimneys on the boiler house, so interiors stay open and huge.",
